  "notes": [
    "Two central dispatch methods move to interp/natives/dispatch.rs. Independent review checked unchanged method content including comments and attributes against committed HEAD, allowing only scoped visibility and formatting. The inline-never attribute, heavy-frame wrappers and iterator-setter recursion shortcut remain in force.",
    "Seven source-lock targets, the general baseline and eight existing property/regexp controls completed before runtime source edits. Candidate controls run serially after all validation processes finish, with no concurrent builds or tests started by this task. General comparison uses unchanged run.py compare and validate_reference at 1.25x. All measured reports are retained.",
    "The eight targeted controls exclude compile/link/boot, use one warmup and five measured rounds, and check completion, results and raw-meter stability. Guest results and raw meter totals agree across revisions.",
    "The GC and allocation method scans include natives/dispatch.rs. The capacity checker explicitly scans that module as well as the historical parent interval, property and regexp modules. A new mutation test rejects both raw Vec::with_capacity and sized vec! reservations in moved dispatch code.",
    "A wrapper comment was corrected from dispatch below to dispatcher because the body now lives in the native module; no wrapper code changed.",
    "This incremental F142 comparison does not establish full 1A performance acceptance against the original decomposition baseline.",
    "Full engine CI passed 1490 tests with 26 ignored over 185 targets; SQLite passed 116 with 3 ignored. All six validation commands exited 0; VM rustdoc reported 61 existing warnings."
  ],
